          "filename": "Stable Block Sheringham Hall 27 August 2014.JPG",
          "caption": "The coachman’s house for Sheringham Hall which was designed by John Adey Repton. The building is a Grade II listed building. The brick built building is faced with pebble flintwork with gault brick quoining. The building is topped with a welsh slate roof which has a central wooden cupola bell turret faced with a clock. This is topped with a gilded weathervane.\n\nIn front of the block is enclosed courtyard  with brick walls. Upper Sheringham,  Norfolk",
